<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Aug   July   June    May   Aug'95</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	    82.5   82.7   82.9   82.1   82.4</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	  90.9   91.2   92.2   90.3   89.6</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks    86.2   91.4   85.1   82.9   82.0</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	82.0   82.0   81.8   82.0   83.0</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products    94.8   93.1   94.1   93.8   93.2</p>
<p> Mining			92.4   90.2   91.1   89.8   89.3</p>
<p> Utilities		   91.8   90.5   92.3   94.1   95.3</p>
<p>Wall Street economists were expecting a 0.4 percent rise in August industrial production and an 83.3 percent capacity use rate.</p>
<p>Motor vehicle assemblies fell in August to a rate of 6.7 million a year for automobiles from 7.0 million in July. For light trucks the assembly rate was down to 5.6 million in August from 6.0 million in July.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles and parts, August industrial output rose 0.6 percent after falling 0.1 percent in July.</p>
<p>The Fed said some of the pickup in August industrial output was a result of weather-related swings in utility output as warmer weather raised electricity use.</p>
